# One command at a time

Riham is learning by running commands. Do not dump a script or a list of commands.

## Required

- Give **exactly one** shell command in a message.
- Put that command in its own fenced `bash` block.
- Say what it does in one short sentence.
- Then stop. Wait for Riham to run it and paste the output (or say it worked / failed).
- Only then give the next command.

## Do not

- Chain commands with `&&` or `;` unless they are one inseparable action (almost never).
- Send `git fetch`, `git checkout`, and `eas build` in the same reply.
- Send a numbered list of commands "for later".
- Ask Riham to run the next command before the current one has finished.

## If npm asks `Ok to proceed? (y)`

Tell Riham to type **`y`** and press Enter. Do not give a different command in that same message.

## Exceptions

A single command may include flags (`npx eas-cli build --platform android --profile preview`). That is still one command.
